KNOWNBUG gcc16 libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ setw inserter converts: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^\[(?!main\.assertion\.2\]).*: FAILURE$
--
Construction of a stream and its ctype facets with the headers of
libstdc++ 16 (tagged libstdcxx16: runs only where the host gcc is 16 or
later, regression/README.md); with gcc 16 the wchar_t facet is reached.
It needed GCC's atomic builtins in C++ (__gnu_cxx::__atomic_add's
__atomic_fetch_add: the CONVERSION ERROR), and the modelled "C" locale
ctype<char> facet (cpp_typecheck_stdlib.cpp) filling the _M_widen and
_M_narrow caches with the identity and setting _M_widen_ok and
_M_narrow_ok ([facet.ctype.char.virtuals]/1, [locale.ctype.virtuals]/11,
13), so ctype<char>::widen needs no virtual call on the modelled object.
Any failed property other than the WRONG assertion is forbidden.  To
check elsewhere, preprocess with g++-16 -E and run cbmc on the .ii file.
